From rth at twiddle.net  Wed Jun  1 21:04:42 2005
From: rth at twiddle.net (Richard Henderson)
Date: Wed, 1 Jun 2005 14:04:42 -0700
Subject: new read-only plt format
Message-ID: <20050601210442.GA5138@twiddle.net>

Apparently SElinux really really doesn't like writable code.  Alan
Modra recently spent a bunch of time redesigning powerpc32 to cope
with this restriction.

It was quite a bit easier for alpha; implementable over a long weekend.
Checked in to head glibc and binutils is support for a new read-only
plt format.  

So if folk are actively working on FC4, I'd appreciate it if they'd 
give the new code a try.



